{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '981,1250p' .task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v5.md\"","aggregated_output":"local-store paths. A network fetch may reject corrupt bytes earlier through\nthe already required transfer fsck, but it MUST NOT turn a known object\nsemantic rejection into availability, cache-hit, or audit success.\n\nAfter a terminal commit passes:\n\n1. the manager requests its one tree ID, recomputes it, and requires actual\n   type `tree`;\n2. it parses each tree as the Git binary sequence\n   `<octal-mode> SP <name-bytes> NUL <H-byte-object-id>`, consuming the entire\n   object with no empty/duplicate name, slash, NUL, `.`/`..`, invalid UTF-8,\n   nonportable component, or platform collision;\n3. it accepts only tree mode `40000` and blob modes `100644`/`100755`; symlink\n   `120000`, gitlink `160000`, unknown modes, and mode/type mismatch fail;\n4. it reads and recomputes every reachable tree and blob, proving every\n   required object locally available without replace, graft, alternate,\n   promisor, lazy-fetch, checkout, attribute, filter, textconv, mailmap, or\n   archive transformation;\n5. it runs section 6.6.3's all-blob detector before materialization or audit;\n6. it materializes exact verified blob bytes into a frozen regular-file\n   snapshot with manager filesystem code, preserving only the executable bit\n   distinction from `100755`/`100644`.\n\nGitlinks fail before reading `.gitmodules`. Parent history, human identity,\ncommit/tag messages, signatures, and extra headers remain untrusted bounded\nmetadata and are never used as provenance.\n\nRequired cross-language semantic fixtures use UTF-8 only for compact display;\nthe parser itself is byte-oriented:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"valid-commit-with-signed-and-extra-headers\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nparent bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\nauthor A U Thor <a@example.test> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C O Mitter <c@example.test> 2 +0000\\ngpgsig -----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n payload\\n -----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\nx-curator-fixture opaque\\n\\nmessage\\r\\nbody\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"valid\",\n    \"tree\": \"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-duplicate-tree-header\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntree bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-misordered-tree-after-parent\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"parent bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\ntree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-missing-header-message-separator\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"tree aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nauthor A <a@b> 1 +0000\\ncommitter C <c@d> 2 +0000\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"valid-signed-annotated-tag\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntype commit\\ntag v1.4.0\\ntagger T Agger <t@example.test> 3 +0000\\n\\nrelease\\n-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\\nopaque\\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected\": \"valid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-duplicate-object-and-type-headers\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nobject bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\ntype commit\\ntype tag\\ntag v1.4.0\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reject-tag-declared-target-type-mismatch\",\n    \"source_paths\": [\"network-private-store\", \"local-inert-copy\"],\n    \"object_type\": \"tag\",\n    \"object_format\": \"sha1\",\n    \"content_utf8\": \"object aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\ntype tag\\ntag v1.4.0\\n\\nmessage\\n\",\n    \"resolved_target_type\": \"commit\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_object_semantics_invalid\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n#### 6.6.3 Exact all-blob Git LFS rejection\n\nThe manager scans every reachable blob exactly once, regardless of path,\nextension, mode, selected build root, `.gitattributes`, or later `go list`\nselection. This happens after object-ID recomputation and before snapshot\nmaterialization, audit, cache lookup, or compiler execution. The detector never\ninvokes `git-lfs`, a filter, or the network.\n\nThe supported parser-family invariant is exactly\n`git-lfs-pointer-parser-v3.7.1`: the decoder and encoder behavior in the\nofficial Git LFS `v3.7.1` `lfs/pointer.go`, exercised by the Git LFS 3.7.1\nbinary in conformance. A different parser family requires a reviewed detector\nrevision. The protocol does not claim that the published pointer specification\nalone describes every byte form accepted by that implementation.\n\nA zero-byte blob is admitted because Git LFS encodes the empty file as empty\nGit content. Every non-empty blob of 1 through 1023 bytes is a candidate.\nExactly 1024 bytes or more is outside both the pinned decoder cutoff and this\ndetector, even if a shorter prefix looks like a pointer.\n\nFor a candidate, manager code applies this bounded compatibility algorithm:\n\n1. Remove the maximal leading and trailing sequence of Unicode White_Space\n   scalar encodings recognized by Go 1.25's `unicode.IsSpace`: ASCII HT, LF,\n   VT, FF, CR, SP; U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000 through U+200A, U+2028,\n   U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, and U+3000. Invalid UTF-8 outside those exact\n   encodings is not trimmed. This is the cross-language definition of the\n   pinned decoder's `bytes.TrimSpace`.\n2. Split the remainder at LF. Remove one terminal CR from each line, as Go's\n   `bufio.ScanLines` does, and ignore empty lines. Embedded CR and invalid\n   UTF-8 remain ordinary bytes.\n3. Each non-empty line must contain an ASCII SP. Split at the first SP only;\n   the bytes before it are `key` and all remaining bytes are `value`.\n4. Required keys occur exactly once and in parser state order:\n   `version`, then `oid`, then `size`. While waiting for any required key, an\n   extension line may occur; no line may occur after `size`.\n5. `version` equals exactly one of:\n   `https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1`,\n   `https://hawser.github.com/spec/v1`, or\n   `http://git-media.io/v/2`.\n6. `oid` equals `sha256:` plus exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal bytes.\n7. `size` is the exact input grammar accepted by Go `strconv.ParseInt` with\n   base 10 and width 64, and its mathematical value is nonnegative. Thus\n   `+1`, `00`, and `01` are accepted noncanonical forms; a negative value,\n   overflow above signed 64-bit, whitespace, or non-decimal byte is not.\n8. An extension key begins exactly `ext-`, one ASCII digit `0` through `9`,\n   `-`, then at least one ASCII `[A-Za-z0-9_]` byte. After that first name\n   byte, every byte other than ASCII SP or LF belongs to the name; there is no\n   end-anchored name regexp. This deliberately covers lowercase/dot/dash,\n   `_`, uppercase, and names whose accepted prefix is followed by punctuation\n   such as `a!`, matching the pinned `\\Aext-\\d{1}-\\w+` behavior. The extension\n   value uses the exact OID grammar from step 6.\n9. Extension entries are first collected by their entire raw key, with a later\n   exact duplicate key replacing the earlier value as in the pinned map.\n   After collection, distinct surviving keys MUST have unique numeric\n   priorities. A repeated exact key is accepted but noncanonical; distinct\n   keys with the same priority are rejected by the pinned family and therefore\n   do not match this detector.\n10. Missing required keys, an unknown non-extension key, malformed OID/size,\n    an extension name not beginning with an ASCII word byte, a bad extension\n    value, or distinct duplicate priorities ends the match.\n\nEvery successful compatibility match is rejected, not merely strict/canonical\nmatches. Classification is diagnostic only:\n\n- `canonical` means the original blob bytes exactly equal the pinned encoder:\n  current version first; surviving extensions sorted by numeric priority and\n  emitted as their raw names; then `oid`, `size`, and one final LF, with no\n  trimming, blank line, duplicate key, or alternate spelling.\n- a non-empty pointer whose parsed size is zero is always\n  `legacy-or-noncanonical`, because the pinned encoder emits an empty blob for\n  size zero;\n- aliases, CRLF, omitted/folded endings, leading/trailing whitespace, blank\n  lines, reordered extension placement, exact duplicate keys, signed/zero-\n  padded sizes, or any other accepted bytes unequal to the encoder are also\n  `legacy-or-noncanonical`.\n\nBoth classifications fail the same stable pre-audit error:\n\n```text\nbuild_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\n```\n\nThe false-positive boundary is closed: only a non-empty blob below 1024 bytes\nthat completes all ten compatibility steps is rejected. A 1024-byte blob,\nunknown version, uppercase/bad OID, missing required key, extension beginning\nwith punctuation, or two distinct extension keys sharing a priority remains\nordinary blob content. The diagnostic may identify classification and path,\nbut MUST NOT print the pointer OID as a fetch instruction. The manager never\nhydrates from `.git/lfs`, an LFS endpoint, a filter, or local operator state.\n\nRequired cross-language fixtures:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"canonical-current-pointer\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"canonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"canonical-extension-name-family\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-lower.dot-dash sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-2-_under sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\next-3-A_B sha256:dddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddddd\\next-4-a! sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"canonical\",\n    \"git_lfs_3_7_1_strict_exit\": 0\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"accepted-crlf-blank-unsorted-and-no-terminal-lf\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"\\r\\nversion https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\r\\next-4-a! sha256:eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee\\r\\n\\r\\next-1-lower sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\r\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\r\\nsize +01\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"accepted-exact-duplicate-key-last-value-wins\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-1-a sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"distinct-duplicate-priority-is-not-accepted\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\next-1-b sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"nonempty-size-zero-is-deliberately-noncanonical\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 0\\n\",\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\",\n    \"git_lfs_3_7_1_strict_exit\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cutoff-1023-after-trim\",\n    \"construction\": {\n      \"prefix_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n      \"pad_byte_hex\": \"20\",\n      \"total_bytes\": 1023\n    },\n    \"expected_error\": \"build_repository_git_lfs_unsupported\",\n    \"classification\": \"legacy-or-noncanonical\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cutoff-1024-is-ordinary\",\n    \"construction\": {\n      \"prefix_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n      \"pad_byte_hex\": \"20\",\n      \"total_bytes\": 1024\n    },\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"near-miss-extension-starts-with-punctuation\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\next-1-!a sha256:bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb\\noid sha256:aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"near-miss-uppercase-oid\",\n    \"bytes_utf8\": \"version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1\\noid sha256:AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\\nsize 1\\n\",\n    \"expected\": \"ordinary-blob\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nNo audit or artifact-cache lookup begins until the object proof, LFS scan,\nmaterialization, whole-snapshot validation, and\n`curator-build-source-v1` digest succeed. Object bytes are transport input, not\nprovenance, and the object store is never agent-facing, runtime-copied, or used\ndirectly as build source.\n\n## 7. Snapshot identity and audit equivalence\n\nThe consuming skill snapshot and each effective external repository snapshot are independent untrusted audit subjects.\n\nFor every external repository selected by the active plan:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
