v4.md against all prior verdicts and primary Git/Git-LFS specifications. Do not edit producer or product/spec/code resources. Reconfirm all previously accepted protocol, identity, audit, output, cache, lifecycle, SSH, signing and future-driver boundaries. Verify the one exact cat-file --batch argv/environment/request/response process is raw, no-network, no-transform, bounded, childless, and sufficient for commit/tag/tree/blob proof on both network and copied local stores; verify manager parsers and hash recomputation close revision/path/filter/replace/lazy indirection. Verify local pack v2/v3 and index-v2 physical grammar, SHA-1/SHA-256 widths/checksums/CRC/large offsets, private staging and stable rejection are interoperable and compatible with the trusted Git reader. Verify the all-reachable-blob LFS detector against official current and cited legacy pointer grammar, cutoff, line ordering/endings/extensions/oid/size rules, false-positive boundary and stable pre-audit error. Validate exact vectors/JSON/source claims. Attach a new v4 verdict resource; set done only if implementation-ready, otherwise route to analysis with exact defects.\\\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\\\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-d2dd94, max_parallel=20)\\\\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260727-d2dd94)\\\\nIndependent external-build-repository architecture v4 verdict: changes requested. V4 closes the prior cat-file child-graph and pack/index-subset findings, but two bounded implementation gaps remain: the LFS detector misses extension spellings accepted as canonical by cited Git LFS 3.7.1, allowing pointer bytes to reach go:embed, and the local cat-file path has no exact commit/tag semantic grammar